  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Alabama received $283M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 725 awards with an average award size of $390K. Obligations fell 98.6% year over year. Current-year totals are partial because fiscal year to date figures are incomplete. The state’s recent totals contrast sharply with prior full fiscal years: FY22 obligations were $15B, FY23 were $16.5B, FY24 were $19.1B, FY25 were $20.6B, and FY26 were $20.2B. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated the largest share in FY2027 to date with $137M, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $87.9M and the Department of Justice with $27.6M. THE BOEING COMPANY received the largest vendor share with $91.3M, and Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations with $91.3M. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 spending compare with prior years?",
        "body": "Alabama obligated $283M in FY2027 to date. Fiscal-year comparisons show a steep drop from prior years: FY26 was $20.2B and FY25 was $20.6B. Obligations fell 98.6% year over year. Current FY2027 totals are partial, so the fiscal-year-to-date number may change as the year progresses."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries lead FY2027 obligations?",
        "body": "National Aeronautics and Space Administration led buying agencies with $137M in obligations, followed by Department of Veterans Affairs with $87.9M and Department of Justice with $27.6M. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing led industries with $91.3M, and Engineering Services followed with $74.4M. THE BOEING COMPANY was the top vendor with $91.3M."
      }
    ]
